# Task accuracy — evidence-first standard (all work)

Applies to **every** task: Mastra, CopilotKit, Next.js, Supabase, CI, docs — not one stack only.

Companions: `ponytail.mdc` (smallest change), `lean.mdc` (lifecycle), `ipixai-dev.mdc` (dev servers).

## Principles

- Verify before changing.
- Evidence over assumptions — never guess.
- One concern per task / PR / commit.
- Preserve architecture consistency.
- Prevent documentation drift.
- Align with Linear, conversion docs, and `origin/main` when a remote exists.
- If unverifiable → write **NOT VERIFIED**.
- Do not reopen completed work or re-recommend already-fixed issues.
- Mitigations are not complete fixes — label them honestly.
- Installed package types win over old iPix code that merely compiles.

## Stage 1 — Scope

Before code:

1. Compare with git HEAD / open PRs.
2. Read related Linear issue + AC when one exists.
3. Classify: ✅ In scope · ⚠️ Related but separate · ❌ Out of scope.

Do not expand scope.

## Stage 2 — Evidence

For every finding, collect from:

1. Current source (`rg`, file read)
2. Installed package / types when API shape is disputed
3. Official docs (Mastra MCP, CopilotKit MCP, Context7)
4. Runtime reproduction when possible (split `dev:ui` / `dev:agent` only)

Classify: ✅ Confirmed · 🟡 Unproven · ⚪ Already fixed · ❌ Incorrect · ⚠️ Out of scope.

**Only implement confirmed, in-scope issues.**

## Stage 3 — Implementation

- One logical change at a time; small commits.
- Prefer reuse / extend (ponytail ladder).
- No drive-by refactors.
- Do not mutate production Supabase.

## Stage 4 — Testing

Focused first (unit / typecheck / lint on touched paths), then broader suite / build as required by lean mode.

## Stage 5 — Verification level (required label)

| Level | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| Unit Verified | Tests only |
| Build Verified | `npm run build` (dev-guard: ports 3000/4111 free) |
| Local Runtime Verified | Split `dev:ui` + `dev:agent` (never combined `npm run dev`) |
| Remote Preview Verified | Preview deploy / remote non-prod |
| Production Verified | Live production evidence |

Never claim production readiness without Production Verified evidence.

## Stage 6 — Docs sync

Before Done: implementation matches `docs/mastra/` and AC. No aspirational checkboxes.

## Stage 7 — Architecture

No duplicate SSOT, no old Worker shims, no unnecessary abstractions.

## Stage 8 — Merge / Done gate

CI green · review threads resolved · auth/RLS when applicable · regression tests when behavior changed · remaining risks named.

## Reporting (handoff)

| Item | Result |
|------|--------|
| Finding | Exact issue |
| Evidence | Code / Docs / Runtime / MCP |
| Classification | Confirmed / Unproven / Already Fixed / Incorrect / Out of Scope |
| Change Made | Files (or none) |
| Regression Test | Added / updated / N/A |
| Validation Level | Unit / Build / Local Runtime / Remote Preview / Production |
| Scope Preserved | Yes / No |
| Remaining Risks | Details |
| Next Action | Details |
